cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DetumbleSim: magnetorquer detumbling, B-dot gain sizing and the controllability gap along the geomagnetic field"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-31"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
url: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/detumblesim"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/detumblesim"
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - attitude control
  - detumbling
  - magnetorquer
  - B-dot
  - CubeSat
  - controllability
abstract: >-
  Research-grade simulation of post-deployment spacecraft detumbling with
  magnetorquers. Rigid-body attitude dynamics driven by a tilted centred-dipole
  geomagnetic field along a circular orbit; B-dot and cross-product control
  laws with per-axis dipole saturation; an orbit-averaged first-order
  detumble-time model validated against the simulator; and quantification of
  the controllability gap along the instantaneous field direction, about which
  a magnetorquer cannot produce torque. Includes a learned B-dot gain
  scheduler benchmarked against three classical gain rules with paired
  confidence intervals. Not flight-qualified and not certified for operational
  use.
